# Explicitly Deferred Extensions

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: After v1; not a release dependency
Dependencies: None

## Purpose

Keep optional ideas visible without letting them inflate the plain-speaker-notes v1.

## Tasks

- [ ] Consider ARM64 and Windows 10 only with current support policy and separate qualification.
- [ ] Reassess macOS/Linux with independent platform contracts; never promise Windows-equivalent exclusion.
- [x] Promote requested background translucency to required task21; it is no longer deferred.
- [ ] Evaluate click-through, acrylic/blur, or nonrectangular visuals only after separate capture/input requalification.
- [ ] Consider multi-note/multi-window support only with a per-surface protection and recovery model.
- [ ] Consider teleprompter/autoscroll, formatting, or slide linkage only after an explicit product request.
- [ ] Consider encrypted recovery, cloud sync, or auto-update only with new threat/data/maintenance decisions.
- [ ] Reopen any item only after owner authorization and create a scoped workstream with evidence gates.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Any promoted idea has a separately approved purpose, risk assessment, and acceptance scope.
- [ ] No deferred item is represented as implemented or required for v1.

## Completion evidence

- None. These are optional candidates, not approved requirements.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-07 - Deferred to preserve a small, honest first release.
